WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.076
Better reflection starts with better questions.

00:00:02.076 --> 00:00:02.735
What happened?

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.711
What was I trying to accomplish?

00:00:04.711 --> 00:00:06.029
What did I expect?

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:07.017
What surprised me?

00:00:07.017 --> 00:00:08.664
What evidence do I have?

00:00:08.664 --> 00:00:11.957
These questions slow the move from emotional reaction to conclusion.

00:00:11.957 --> 00:00:17.227
They help separate the event itself from the first story the mind creates about the event.

00:00:17.227 --> 00:00:18.874
Assumption questions are especially useful.

00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:23.156
What did I assume about the task, the user, the system, the timeline,

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.132
the team, or my own skill?

00:00:25.132 --> 00:00:28.426
Which assumptions were supported by evidence, and which were guesses?

00:00:28.426 --> 00:00:31.390
Many failures are not caused by lack of effort.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:35.343
They are caused by reasonable-looking assumptions that were never tested soon enough.

00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:37.319
Outcome questions connect reflection to improvement.

00:00:37.319 --> 00:00:37.978
What worked?

00:00:37.978 --> 00:00:38.637
What failed?

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:39.625
What was lucky?

00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:40.613
What was repeatable?

00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:42.918
What would I do differently next time?

00:00:42.918 --> 00:00:46.212
What should become a checklist, pattern, default, or warning sign?

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:50.165
These questions turn reflection into a practical diagnosis rather than a general

00:00:50.165 --> 00:00:52.470
feeling that something was good or bad.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.446
Blame questions usually produce weaker learning.

00:00:54.446 --> 00:00:55.764
Who is at fault?

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:57.740
Why did I mess this up?

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.716
Why did they not know better?

00:00:59.716 --> 00:01:02.681
These questions narrow attention and often make people defensive.

00:01:02.681 --> 00:01:04.986
Useful reflective questions stay specific and action-oriented.

00:01:04.986 --> 00:01:08.280
They ask what the situation teaches, what can be improved,

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.244
and how the next attempt can be better supported.

00:01:11.244 --> 00:01:15.197
The tone matters because people are more likely to learn when the

00:01:15.197 --> 00:01:18.820
question gives them room to be accurate instead of merely protective.
